WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.425
This is CrossCart.

2
00:00:01.838 --> 00:00:03.088
Let AI compare.

3
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:04.575
You keep the final say.

4
00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:06.525
A shopping agent that asks you

5
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.738
to approve one exact deal, before any payment.

6
00:00:12.538 --> 00:00:14.825
First, the buyer asks in Cantonese

7
00:00:14.838 --> 00:00:17.725
for headphones under eighteen
hundred Hong Kong dollars,

8
00:00:18.088 --> 00:00:19.188
with official warranty

9
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.125
and delivery within two days.

10
00:00:21.513 --> 00:00:23.538
CrossCart interprets the request,

11
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:25.213
and the buyer confirms it.

12
00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.888
The cheapest offer has a third-party warranty.

13
00:00:28.288 --> 00:00:29.713
So it fails the requirement.

14
00:00:32.481 --> 00:00:34.275
Merchant A meets the requirements

15
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:37.157
at seventeen forty-nine, including delivery.

16
00:00:37.516 --> 00:00:39.576
Now the buyer approves this exact deal.

17
00:00:39.958 --> 00:00:43.199
Product, seller, payee, amount and terms

18
00:00:43.199 --> 00:00:44.078
are recorded together.

19
00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.513
The agent compares.

20
00:00:45.872 --> 00:00:47.620
Server rules control the payment.

21
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.113
Next, the buyer opens
official Stripe test Checkout

22
00:00:53.525 --> 00:00:55.788
and enters synthetic test details.

23
00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.300
Stripe authorizes the approved amount.

24
00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.525
Before capture,

25
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.438
CrossCart checks the mandate
and merchant quote again.

26
00:01:02.838 --> 00:01:04.838
This is the actual Stripe sandbox.

27
00:01:05.213 --> 00:01:06.913
No real money or goods move.

28
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.725
Payment is captured.

29
00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:12.538
The demo order is confirmed.

30
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.400
These are separate states,

31
00:01:14.588 --> 00:01:15.650
with a traceable record.

32
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.775
You can inspect the buyer's approval

33
00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:20.938
and the rules checked before payment and capture.

34
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.913
The browser message alone isn't payment proof.

35
00:01:25.488 --> 00:01:26.700
What if the price changes?

36
00:01:27.125 --> 00:01:29.388
The buyer approved seventeen forty-nine.

37
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.413
The current offer is eighteen forty-nine.

38
00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:34.650
CrossCart stops before Checkout.

39
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.675
Payment is not executed.

40
00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.963
The original approval stays unchanged.

41
00:01:40.363 --> 00:01:42.588
A different deal needs a fresh decision.

42
00:01:47.493 --> 00:01:49.750
And if the merchant fails after capture?

43
00:01:50.132 --> 00:01:51.196
The order stays failed.

44
00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.557
CrossCart tracks recovery separately,

45
00:01:53.963 --> 00:01:56.486
and retrieves the same-charge refund from Stripe.

46
00:01:56.856 --> 00:01:58.777
Only then does it show refund confirmed.

47
00:02:00.488 --> 00:02:02.088
Now compare the same task.

48
00:02:02.563 --> 00:02:03.388
Three offers.

49
00:02:03.788 --> 00:02:04.775
The same choice.

50
00:02:05.188 --> 00:02:08.438
The manual layout takes four navigation actions.

51
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.525
CrossCart takes one selection.

52
00:02:10.925 --> 00:02:12.813
This measures the comparison stage,

53
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.850
with shared approval and Checkout excluded.

54
00:02:16.275 --> 00:02:18.213
Browser time is visible,

55
00:02:18.613 --> 00:02:20.013
but it isn't a human study.

56
00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.750
The judge guide links dated primary sources

57
00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.375
for processing fees, card rewards and Clubpoints.

58
00:02:28.775 --> 00:02:30.938
The fee estimate belongs to the merchant.

59
00:02:31.338 --> 00:02:34.025
Reward eligibility is unverified,

60
00:02:34.425 --> 00:02:37.263
so no rebate or points discount is subtracted

61
00:02:37.263 --> 00:02:38.750
from the buyer's approved total.

62
00:02:42.513 --> 00:02:46.013
The public demo runs on Vercel HTTPS,

63
00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.875
with a persistent Neon ledger.

64
00:02:48.275 --> 00:02:50.513
A signed webhook completed an order

65
00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.463
even without the browser return.

66
00:02:52.875 --> 00:02:54.763
Products and orders are synthetic.

67
00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.950
HKT integration is the next proposed step.
